Chapter: MonopolyWasm
  cites Games chapter Monopoly
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Monopoly, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Four players and twenty-eight properties, each a
 record of its own, are far past an i32.

 `mono-set-player` and `mono-set-prop` write with `list-set-at`, which
 mutates in place, so a turn writes through to the caller's lists. Both
 lists hold RECORDS, and the records are rebuilt rather than mutated in
 these two functions, so copying the lists is enough here; the deeper copy
 Hex War needs is not required, and the grader measures that rather than
 assuming it.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  mo-copy-players : List MonopolyPlayer, Integer, Integer, List MonopolyPlayer -> List MonopolyPlayer
  mo-copy-players (src) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else mo-copy-players src (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  mo-copy-props : List PropertyState, Integer, Integer, List PropertyState -> List PropertyState
  mo-copy-props (src) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else mo-copy-props src (i + 1) n (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  mo-copy-state : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mo-copy-state (s) =
    MonopolyState {
      players = mo-copy-players (s.players) 0 (list-length (s.players)) [],
      properties = mo-copy-props (s.properties) 0 (list-length (s.properties)) [],
      current-player = s.current-player,
      turn-number = s.turn-number,
      game-over = s.game-over,
      winner = s.winner,
      num-players = s.num-players,
      phase = s.phase,
      pending = s.pending,
      last-roll = s.last-roll
    }

Section: The Browser Interface

  mo-wasm-new : Integer, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mo-wasm-new (seed) (players) = mono-init seed players

 `mono-do-turn` ENDS a turn, advancing to the next player itself. This
 wrapper used to call `mono-advance-turn` on top of it, so every step of
 the page advanced twice and half the table never took a turn: with four
 players, two of them sat still for a whole game while the counters kept
 reading as a game being played. Nothing that counts turns, cash or
 properties can see a player being skipped.

  mo-wasm-step : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mo-wasm-step (s) (seed) =
    if s.game-over then s
    else mono-do-turn (mo-copy-state s) (rng-new seed)

Section: Taking A Turn Yourself

 A turn is a roll and then, when the square is worth deciding about, a
 choice. `mo-wasm-roll` stops at the offer; `mo-wasm-take` and
 `mo-wasm-leave` are the two ways past it, and both end the turn.

  mo-wasm-roll : MonopolyState, Integer -> MonopolyState
  mo-wasm-roll (s) (seed) =
    if s.game-over then s
    else mono-roll (mo-copy-state s) (rng-new seed)

  mo-wasm-take : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mo-wasm-take (s) = mono-take (mo-copy-state s) (s.current-player)

  mo-wasm-leave : MonopolyState -> MonopolyState
  mo-wasm-leave (s) = mono-leave (mo-copy-state s) (s.current-player)

  mo-wasm-phase : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-phase (s) = s.phase

  mo-wasm-offered : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-offered (s) = mono-offered s

  mo-wasm-last-roll : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-last-roll (s) = s.last-roll

  mo-wasm-can-roll : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-can-roll (s) =
    if s.game-over then 0 else if s.phase == 0 then 1 else 0

  mo-wasm-can-decide : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-can-decide (s) (player) =
    if mono-can-decide s player then 1 else 0

 What the offer would cost you, and what you would still be holding after
 it. A page that showed the price without the balance would be asking for a
 decision it had not given you the numbers for.

  mo-wasm-offer-cost : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-offer-cost (s) =
    if s.phase /= 1 then (-1)
    else if s.pending < 0 then (-1)
    else (list-at (s.properties) (s.pending)).cost

  mo-wasm-offer-color : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-offer-color (s) =
    if s.phase /= 1 then (-1)
    else if s.pending < 0 then (-1)
    else (list-at (s.properties) (s.pending)).color

 A BOARD SPACE and a PROPERTY INDEX are different numbers, and both are
 different again from a player. Forty spaces hold twenty-two properties, so
 `mo_owner` takes 0..21 and a page drawing the board has 0..39 in its hand.
 Without this export a page has to guess, and the arcade's did: it read the
 board space as a property index AND as a player, so the board has never
 coloured a single owned square in.

  mo-wasm-prop-at : Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-prop-at (space) =
    if space < 0 then (-1)
    else if space >= 40 then (-1)
    else if mono-is-property space then mono-prop-index space
    else (-1)

  mo-wasm-offer-space : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-offer-space (s) =
    if s.phase /= 1 then (-1)
    else if s.pending < 0 then (-1)
    else mo-space-of (s.pending) 0

  mo-space-of : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mo-space-of (pi) (space) =
    if space >= 40 then (-1)
    else if mo-wasm-prop-at space == pi then space
    else mo-space-of pi (space + 1)

  mo-wasm-offer-rent : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-offer-rent (s) =
    if s.phase /= 1 then (-1)
    else if s.pending < 0 then (-1)
    else (list-at (s.properties) (s.pending)).base-rent

  mo-wasm-players : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-players (s) = s.num-players

  mo-wasm-cash : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-cash (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= s.num-players then (-1)
    else (mono-get-player s i).cash

  mo-wasm-position : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-position (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= s.num-players then (-1)
    else (mono-get-player s i).position

  mo-wasm-in-jail : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-in-jail (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= s.num-players then (-1)
    else if (mono-get-player s i).in-jail then 1 else 0

  mo-wasm-props : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-props (s) = list-length (s.properties)

  mo-wasm-prop-owner : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-prop-owner (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-2)
    else if i >= list-length (s.properties) then (-2)
    else (list-at (s.properties) i).owner

  mo-wasm-prop-cost : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-prop-cost (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length (s.properties) then (-1)
    else (list-at (s.properties) i).cost

  mo-wasm-prop-color : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-prop-color (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length (s.properties) then (-1)
    else (list-at (s.properties) i).color

  mo-wasm-owned : MonopolyState, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-owned (s) (i) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= s.num-players then (-1)
    else list-length ((mono-get-player s i).owned-properties)

  mo-wasm-owned-at : MonopolyState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mo-wasm-owned-at (s) (i) (k) =
    if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= s.num-players then (-1)
    else let owned = (mono-get-player s i).owned-properties
    in if k < 0 then (-1)
    else if k >= list-length owned then (-1)
    else list-at owned k

  mo-wasm-cur : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-cur (s) = s.current-player

  mo-wasm-turn : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-turn (s) = s.turn-number

  mo-wasm-done : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-done (s) = if s.game-over then 1 else 0

  mo-wasm-winner : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-winner (s) = s.winner

 Bankruptcy is rare in this engine (games-backlog GAME-8: no trading, so a
 colour group is only ever assembled by luck of the dice), and `mono-loop`
 resolves an undecided game by capping the turn count and awarding it to the
 richest player. A page stepping the state itself has to do the same, so the
 richest player is exported rather than left for the page to work out from
 cash and property.

  mo-wasm-richest : MonopolyState -> Integer
  mo-wasm-richest (s) = mono-richest s (s.num-players)

  mo-wasm-turn-cap : Integer
  mo-wasm-turn-cap = 601

